#
# Frames the NMEA 2000 analyzer must refuse, plus one valid live-form frame
# (candump without -l, which prints "[8]" instead of "#").
#
# candump prints a standard (11-bit) identifier as %03x and an extended
# (29-bit) one as %08X, so the frame shape is recoverable from the text. An
# 11-bit identifier is Quick, and pushing it through the J1939 bit layout would
# invent a PGN, a priority and a source address that the frame does not carry.
# An error frame ("##") has no decodable payload. Run with -fixtime so the
# error log is reproducible.
#
  can0  09F80107   [8]  24 35 3C 00 00 C0 C0 C0
  vcan0  00000100##1000000000000000
(1502979135.506111) vcan0 6C1#C1186B0000000200
  vcan0  6C1   [8]  C1 18 6B 00 00 00 02 00
